            <ArticleTitle>Horner syndrome with causalgia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>534-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A previously healthy man presented with burning pain in the chest wall and arm; there was Horner syndrome on the same side. After extensive investigation, the disorder was attributed to a foraminal osteophyte involving the left T1 spinal root.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
